WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.990
1565.

2
00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:06.340
An Italian writer, Cinthio,
tells of a Moor and his wife,

3
00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:08.060
over a long time.

4
00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:13.220
Shakespeare adds a Turkish threat, and
squeezes it into two nights and a day.

5
00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:14.940
A ship at the quay.

6
00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:18.120
Then a bedchamber, lit by one candle.

7
00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:20.310
He threw away months of story.

8
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.420
Why squeeze it so tight?

9
00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:25.130
In this mission, you'll
see what Shakespeare kept,

10
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.260
and changed, from an Italian prose tale.

11
00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:31.630
You'll watch a comedy in
Act 1 tip into tragedy,

12
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.350
and test Bradley's view that
the conflict "begins late".

13
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.460
And you'll find a hidden
second clock: "What,

14
00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:39.640
keep a week away?

15
00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.560
Seven days and nights?"

16
00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:45.900
Your mission: work out why
Shakespeare squeezed it into two days.
